flowchart TD
    %% Send side
    ATTACH([User attaches a file to a message]) --> PICK[GUI picks the file · platform chooser]
PICK --> COPY[Core copies it into the store, or references it in place · keep-a-copy checkbox<br>block hashes → fileId · classify]
    COPY --> MSG[Publish message with attachment references<br>notification only — no key, no chunk params]
COPY --> CLASS{file class}
MSG --> CLASS
CLASS -- " small (≤ smallFileMaxBytes · a network value) " --> FAN[Send fans out: one transfer per device of the account]
CLASS -- " large (no upper bound) " --> NOPUSH([nothing pushed · each device decides to fetch])

FAN --> MARKER[OFFER marker per device · direct link first<br>sealed half: fileId + block list + this transfer's own key, ratchet-encrypted]

MARKER -- " ACK (accepted) " --> CHUNKS[Chunk rows in the outbox · windowed · messages go first<br>routing encrypts plaintext from the orchestrator's source<br>chunk ACK = decrypted + durably staged]
    MARKER -- "DECLINED (relay full)" --> NEXTRELAY[Next relay or re-offer later]
    MARKER -- "DECLINED (target)" --> DEAD([send to that device terminally DECLINED])
MARKER -- " other terminal NACK " --> ENDEDM([transfer ENDED · REQUEST recovers])
    CHUNKS -- "all ACKed" --> PUSHED((push complete))
CHUNKS -- " link closed · no link · no chunk ACK at all for chunkAckTimeout " --> REM[Remainder = suffix after the<br>highest contiguous ACKed prefix]
    REM --> DEPOSIT[Deposit once per transfer · identical set<br>at every relay RelaySelectionPolicy returns]
    DEPOSIT --> ADM{Admission against<br>the storage pledge}
    ADM -- accepted --> HOLD
    ADM -- DECLINED --> OUT([that relay is out · one jump<br>the sender never chases])
    HOLD["Store ciphertext chunks in the relay store<br>PK (transferId, chunkIndex) · signature verified<br>dead transferId or out-of-range index → DECLINED at the door"]
    HOLD --> WHOLE{Whole covered suffix?}
    WHOLE -- no --> TTL[Reservation TTL cleans up<br>never pushed, never offered]
    WHOLE -- yes --> FOFFER[OFFER marker to the target<br>stored OFFER payload replayed verbatim]
    FOFFER -- ACK --> FWD[Forward chunks from the store<br>per-chunk ACKs delete rows]
    FOFFER -- "DECLINED (no space)" --> DROP([relay drops the transfer · quota freed])
    FWD --> DRAINED((transfer row dropped when drained))


    %% Teardown
    PUSHED --> TEARDOWN[Receiver READY → COMPLETE to every live transfer author<br>each resolves its transfer and cancels its deposits]
    TEARDOWN --> DONE([transfer COMPLETED])

    %% Pull path
    MSG -. "synced / processed by any device" .-> TRIG
TRIG{Message references a fileId · no complete local file ·<br>no progressing transfer · small: push window ·<br>large: auto-download limit or user click} -- yes --> CAND[One candidate at a time · serve gate at the holder<br>sender devices, then own-account siblings]
CAND -- " small " --> REQ[REQUEST envelope · sealed, direct-only<br>ACK → waiting for the OFFER · DECLINED → next candidate]
CAND -- " large " --> PULL[Requester opens a WebRTC session and a file channel<br>PULL fileId + fromOffset = checkpointed P<br>PULL_OK with the block list · DECLINED → next candidate]
REQ -- " OFFER (fresh transferId · fresh key) " --> SERVE[Holder serves the suffix from the floor-aligned<br>boundary below the requester's lowest missing byte<br>checks each block as it reads]
PULL -- " PULL_OK " --> STREAM[Holder sends plain DATA frames in order · block-checked<br>no envelope, no key, no transferId · DTLS protects the channel<br>PROGRESS at checkpoints · credit window · ends with the channel]
STREAM -- " session dropped " --> CAND
PULL -- " no session possible " --> NOCONN([no direct connection · shown to the user · never over Tor])
NOPUSH -. " message lands" .-> TRIG
CAND -- " all DECLINED / expired " --> UNAV([file unavailable · re-openable])
SERVE --> MERGE[Receiver merges into fileId-scoped byte coverage<br>blocks verified at checkpoints → READY → COMPLETE to live authors]
    FWD -. delivered .-> MERGE
    STREAM -. delivered .-> MERGE
    CHUNKS -. delivered .-> MERGE
MERGE -. " prefix stalls for fileStallTimeout · live transfers are kept " .-> TRIG
